I've determined a container like `relative w-full max-w-4xl`, with the buttons inside (either absolute or flex), is a promising path. Examining the structure, I note the container is `min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center justify-center`, with buttons as siblings to the central card div. I'm thinking of wrapping both in a `div className="relative w-full max-w-4xl flex justify-center"`. Now, absolute positioning will be relative to that container. I'm exploring various wrapper widths (max-w-md, max-w-2xl, max-w-6xl). The user's input, "próximos ao logo central," might mean moving the buttons into the card's header, though that could crowd it.


